Wrote coder-3.json with one row for `religious-freedom`. The only usable evidence was Clere's Nay vote (House Roll Call 305) on SB 101 (2015), Indiana's RFRA — a single-subject bill whose compelling-interest/least-restrictive-means standard matches rung 4's general exemption language. Since a No vote only rules out that broad standard without establishing a narrower rung, I coded the row BLANK/`direction-only` rather than guessing a chair, and flagged the RFRA "fix" bill (SB 50) and any first-person Clere statement as `needs_source`.
